# Exports Section

## Purpose

Defines the Exports section of the MAM specification. The section declares the classes, functions, constants, and types that form the public API of the module.

## Inputs

| Name | Type | Required | Description |
|------|------|----------|-------------|
| content | string | Yes | Full MAM module text that contains the section |
| exports | list | No | Export declarations to validate directly |

## Outputs

| Name | Type | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| exports | list | Extracted public API declarations |
| valid | bool | Whether the section passes validation |
| errors | list | Validation errors found in the exports |

## Capabilities

### validate

Checks export names, duplicates, type annotations, and documentation.

### extract

Pulls the export declarations out of the section body.

### document

Renders the exports into documentation for the public API.

## Rules

- Export only the public API, never internal implementation.
- Use descriptive names that follow language conventions.
- Give every export a description.
- Include type signatures when possible.
- Use consistent formatting for all exports.
- List each export only once.

## Workflow

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Content] --> B[Extract]
    B --> C[Validate]
    C --> D[Document]
    D --> E[Output]
```

## Python

```python
import re

def validate_export_name(name: str, export_type: str) -> bool:
    if export_type == "function":
        return bool(re.match(r"^[a-z_][a-z0-9_]*$", name))
    if export_type == "constant":
        return bool(re.match(r"^[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*$", name))
    return bool(re.match(r"^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*$", name))

def check_duplicate_exports(exports: list) -> list:
    seen = set()
    duplicates = []
    for export in exports:
        name = export.split(" ")[0].strip("`")
        if name in seen:
            duplicates.append(name)
        seen.add(name)
    return duplicates

def validate_type_annotation(annotation: str) -> bool:
    return bool(re.match(r"^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_\.,\s\[\]\(\)]*$", annotation))

def extract_exports(content: str) -> list:
    exports = []
    in_section = False
    for line in content.split("\n"):
        if line.strip().startswith("## Exports"):
            in_section = True
            continue
        if in_section and line.startswith("##"):
            break
        if in_section and line.strip().startswith("- "):
            exports.append(line.strip()[2:].strip("`"))
    return exports

def validate_exports(exports: list) -> list:
    errors = []
    for export in exports:
        name = export.split(" ")[0].strip("`")
        if not validate_export_name(name, "function"):
            errors.append("Invalid export name: " + name)
    for dup in check_duplicate_exports(exports):
        errors.append("Duplicate export: " + dup)
    return errors

def generate_docs(exports: list) -> str:
    docs = "## Public API\n\n"
    for export in exports:
        docs += "- " + export + "\n"
    return docs
```

## Tests

### Input

```yaml
content: |
  ## Exports

  - verify_token - Verify token validity
  - hash_password - Hash password securely
  - DEFAULT_TIMEOUT - Default timeout in seconds
```

### Expected

```yaml
valid: true
errors: []
```

```python
def test_exports():
    exports = ["verify_token", "hash_password", "DEFAULT_TIMEOUT"]
    assert validate_export_name("verify_token", "function")
    assert validate_export_name("DEFAULT_TIMEOUT", "constant")
    assert validate_exports(exports) == []
    assert check_duplicate_exports(exports) == []
    assert "Public API" in generate_docs(exports)
```

## Examples

### Functions

```markdown
- verify_token(token: str) -> bool - Verify token validity
- hash_password(password: str) -> str - Hash password securely
- generate_salt() -> bytes - Generate random salt
```

### Constants

```markdown
- DEFAULT_TIMEOUT - Default timeout (30 seconds)
- MAX_RETRY_ATTEMPTS - Maximum retry attempts (3)
- API_VERSION - API version string
```

